---
/*
 * Terms.
 *
 * The last of the four footer links that went nowhere. Kept deliberately short
 * and in the same voice as the rest of the site: a wall of unreadable clauses
 * protects nobody, because nobody reads it and a term nobody has read is a term
 * that will be argued about anyway.
 *
 * The numbers come from the same constants the checkout uses, so the contract
 * and the code cannot disagree.
 */
import PolicyPage from '../components/PolicyPage.astro';
import { FREE_SHIPPING_OVER, SHIPPING_FLAT, VND_PER_USD } from '../lib/orders';
import { PAYMENT_WINDOW_MINUTES, RETURNS_WINDOW_DAYS, SHOP_ADDRESS, SHOP_EMAIL } from '../lib/shop';

const rate = new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US').format(VND_PER_USD);
const payWindowHours = Math.round(PAYMENT_WINDOW_MINUTES / 60);
---

<PolicyPage
  title="Terms"
  eyebrow="The agreement"
  description="The terms you and I are working under when you buy something here — pricing, payment, delivery, returns and the limits of what I promise."
  intro="Short, and in plain words. Buying something from this shop means agreeing to what is on this page."
  updated="2026-08-28"
>
  <h2>Who you are dealing with</h2>

  <p>
    ZippyZack, a one-person crochet workshop at {SHOP_ADDRESS.join(', ')}, reachable at{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${SHOP_EMAIL}`}>{SHOP_EMAIL}</a>. "I" and "me" below mean that workshop; "you"
    means whoever is placing the order.
  </p>

  <h2>Placing an order</h2>

  <p>
    Adding something to a basket is not an order, and an order is not accepted until the payment
    lands. Until then nothing is reserved for you — stock is drawn down at the moment the transfer
    is confirmed, so it is possible for the last of something to sell while you are at the payment
    screen.
  </p>

  <p>
    If that happens, you will not be left out of pocket: I will either restock and send it, or refund
    you in full. It is a rare situation and it is dealt with by hand.
  </p>

  <p>
    A payment link is good for <strong>{payWindowHours} hours</strong>. After that the order is
    cancelled automatically and you are free to place a new one.
  </p>

  <p>
    I may decline or cancel an order — a listing that was priced wrongly, stock that turns out not to
    exist, or an address I cannot post to. If money has already been taken it goes straight back.
  </p>

  <h2>Prices and currency</h2>

  <p>
    The catalogue is priced in <strong>US dollars</strong>. Payment settles in{' '}
    <strong>Vietnamese dong</strong> through payOS, converted at a fixed rate I set — currently
    ₫{rate} to the dollar. Both figures are shown at checkout before you commit, and the dong figure
    is what actually leaves your account.
  </p>

  <p>
    That rate is deliberately a number I choose rather than a live market feed, so you are never
    quoted one amount and charged another because a rate moved while you were deciding. It is
    reviewed from time to time and can change for future orders, never for one already placed.
  </p>

  <p>
    Shipping is <strong>${SHIPPING_FLAT.toFixed(2)}</strong>, or free over{' '}
    <strong>${FREE_SHIPPING_OVER.toFixed(2)}</strong>. Any import duty or tax charged on the way into
    your country is yours to pay — I have no way to know or collect it in advance.
  </p>

  <p>
    Prices can change at any time. The price you were shown at checkout is the price of your order.
  </p>

  <h2>Payment</h2>

  <p>
    By VietQR bank transfer through payOS. No card details are handled by this site. If a transfer
    arrives for less than the order total, the order is held rather than shipped and I will contact
    you to sort out the difference.
  </p>

  <h2>Delivery</h2>

  <p>
    Delivery times on the <a href="/shipping">shipping page</a> are honest estimates from experience,
    not guarantees, and once a parcel is with a courier its progress is out of my hands. Risk passes
    to you on delivery — until the parcel reaches you, a loss in transit is my problem to solve.
  </p>

  <p>
    An address typed wrongly is the one case I cannot fix for free. Check it at checkout; if you spot
    a mistake, email me immediately and I will change it if the parcel has not gone.
  </p>

  <h2>Handmade means varied</h2>

  <p>
    Everything here is made by hand from natural materials. Dye lots differ, screens render colour
    differently, and no two pieces come out identical. Small variations in colour, size and texture
    are the nature of the thing rather than defects.
  </p>

  <p>
    Where a listing gives measurements, treat them as close rather than exact. If a piece needs to
    fit something precisely, ask before ordering.
  </p>

  <h2>Returns</h2>

  <p>
    Set out in full on the <a href="/shipping">shipping and returns page</a>, which forms part of
    these terms. In short: {RETURNS_WINDOW_DAYS} days from arrival, anything wrong with the order is
    put right at my cost, and a change of mind is fine on unused goods with return postage yours.
    Wound or worked yarn, made-to-order pieces and digital patterns cannot come back.
  </p>

  <h2>Patterns and images</h2>

  <p>
    Patterns bought or downloaded here are for your own personal use. You are welcome to sell
    finished items you have made from them — that is what they are for. You may not resell,
    redistribute or republish the pattern itself.
  </p>

  <p>
    The photographs, illustrations, text and design of this site are mine. The pattern generator
    produces images from your prompt using a third-party AI model; do not rely on generated images or
    generated instructions being accurate, original, or safe to use commercially.
  </p>

  <h2>What I do not promise</h2>

  <p>
    The site is provided as it is. I keep it working and accurate, but I cannot promise it will never
    be down, never contain a mistake, or that a listing is free of typos.
  </p>

  <p>
    If something goes wrong with an order, what I owe you is capped at what you paid for that order.
    I am not liable for indirect losses — a deadline missed because a parcel was late, a project
    abandoned, and so on. Nothing here limits liability for anything that cannot lawfully be limited,
    including death, personal injury or fraud.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes and disputes</h2>

  <p>
    These terms may change; the version in force for your order is the one published when you placed
    it. If any part of this page turns out to be unenforceable, the rest still stands.
  </p>

  <p>
    Vietnamese law governs any dispute, and the courts of Vietnam have jurisdiction. Before it ever
    gets that far, though, <a href={`mailto:${SHOP_EMAIL}`}>email me</a>. Almost everything is
    fixable in one message.
  </p>
</PolicyPage>
